# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. the two claims
# Claim 1 - the border pixels are present after and absent before. Count of differing pixels of the
# 400x400 frame, from the two PPM rasters (the recipe is a pixel count, checked against a one-pixel
# control that reports 1):
#   convert before/<v>.ppm after/<v>.ppm -compose difference -composite -threshold 0 \
#     -format "%[fx:int(mean*w*h+0.5)]" info:
#
#   view D  368 of 160000 (0.230 %)   difference bbox x 0..86, y 179..346
#   view B  690 of 160000 (0.431 %)   difference bbox x 200..399, y 76..387
#   view E  564 of 160000 (0.352 %)   difference bbox x 95..239, y 156..277
#   view A    0 of 160000
#
# View D: the difference bbox starts at x=0 and spans y 179..346, which are the two places where the
# projected ring of way 367958283 crosses the left viewport edge (y=179.3 and y=346.6): the difference
# is the stretch of that area's border that enters and leaves through the viewport's left edge.
# View B: same shape on the right edge (crossings at y=77.7 and y=308.9, difference bbox x 200..399).
#
# The colours of the differing pixels: the before image shows the map content, the after image the
# border of the area. Most frequent (before -> after) pairs, view D:
#   (235,235,235) -> (179,199,170)  9 px      (235,235,235) -> (170,194,160)  6 px
#   (235,235,235) -> (210,219,206)  5 px      (235,235,235) -> (173,195,163)  5 px
# View B (fence, colour #aaaaaa of its AREA.BORDER):
#   (241,238,233) -> (239,236,231) 19 px      (241,238,233) -> (223,221,217) 15 px
#   (241,238,233) -> (214,212,209) 12 px
#
# How the difference was checked to lie on that area's border and not to be scattered: every differing
# pixel was set against the projected OSM ring of the way, and its distance to the closest ring segment
# computed (python over the two PPM rasters):
#   view D  max distance 0.78 px,  differing pixels farther than 4 px: 0
#   view B  max distance 1.25 px,  differing pixels farther than 4 px: 0
#   view E  max distance 0.75 px,  differing pixels farther than 4 px: 0
# (the projection of the render matches the formula above to below one pixel, which also shows that the
# database carries the ring of the OSM way unchanged)
#
# Claim 2 - the output strictly inside the view is unchanged. The whole difference bounding box lies
# outside a sub-rectangle of the frame that keeps the map content in it, and that sub-rectangle
# differs in no pixel:
#   view D  crop 280x400+120+0 (x 120..399, 33 px right of the difference bbox): 0 differing pixels
#   view B  crop 200x400+0+0 (x 0..199, the left half): 0 differing pixels
#   convert before/<v>.ppm -crop <geometry> +repage b.png; convert after/<v>.ppm -crop <geometry> +repage a.png
#   convert b.png a.png -compose difference -composite -threshold 0 -format "%[fx:int(mean*w*h+0.5)]" info:
# Together with the corridor check of claim 1 (no differing pixel farther than 0.78 / 1.25 px from the
# border of the identified area) this says: the only pixels that change are the border pixels of the
# area whose border crosses the viewport edge; the rest of the frame, the interior of that area
